This function is supposed to check if two strings are anagrams of each other, ignoring case and spaces, but it incorrectly returns False for some pairs that ARE anagrams under that definition (e.g. it should treat 'Dormitory' and 'dirty room' as anagrams, but doesn't).

def is_anagram(a, b):
    return sorted(a) == sorted(b)

Identify the bug and explain the fix.
